 in both procedure arms.\",\n    \"Both arms of the procedure honour the unit: the workflow collapses each digester to one mean before inference, and the permutation test permutes the 10 digester-level means (C(10,5) = 252 splits of units), never the 40 cycle rows; treatment labels are constant within unit so no unit is split across arms.\",\n    \"The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue: it states n = 10 with one analysed value per digester, lists the 10 digester means (verified against the raw data, e.g. D01 = (211.2+220.4+216.9+225.5)/4 = 218.50), reports the group comparison on 5 vs 5 digester means, and explicitly notes that the 40 rows are not 40 independent observations.\",\n    \"The reported statistics check out at the unit level: difference 261.80 - 221.20 = 40.60, and with completely separated groups the two-sided exact permutation p-value is 2/252 = 0.0079, matching the [selected-result] claim of inference on 10 independent digesters.\",\n    \"No lock was minted (NO LOCK MINTED), so no unit-key authorization exists, and none can follow from the declaration alone; a declaration by itself never authorizes a unit key.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":8429,"ttft_stream_ms":1816,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":16487,"uuid":"71c77146-422b-4e50-8882-eeea38bd1db0"}
